FFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core: add a versioned, locked, atomic machine-state store for persistent[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]feature-flag booleans in sase-core, expose strict PyO3 read and set [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bindings, and prove concurrency, corruption, downgrade, and durability [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]behavior.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Adopt the released core binding floor[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]floor[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]floor: wait for the core release, raise sase's sase-core-rs dependency [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]floor, refresh the lockfile and editable install, and smoke-test the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]published bindings before Python callers land.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared Python resolution and mutation facade[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]runtime[dim] · [dim][/dim]after floor[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]runtime: add the thin typed Python adapter, insert saved machine [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]preferences into feature-flag resolution at the designed precedence, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]synchronize process transport after writes, and return one structured [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mutation outcome used by every frontend.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Persistent flag enable and disable commands[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after runtime[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli: add sorted sase flag disable and enable commands with rich and JSON[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]results, completion, idempotent shared mutations, and the existing AXE [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]restart machinery, including clear partial-success reporting.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Beautiful Config Flags pane and controlled restart flow[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]tui[dim] · [dim][/dim]after runtime[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui: create the default-on sunset rollout flag and its live call site, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add the lazy Config > Flags list/detail pane with filtering, provenance,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]removal metadata, confirmation and narrow layouts, and apply successful [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]toggles through the existing proc-aware ACE plus AXE restart path.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Integrated documentation, visual coverage, and release [/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]verification[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]polish[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli, tui[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]polish: align all user documentation and help, exercise the complete CLI[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and TUI journeys including both rollout-flag states and restart [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]failures, refresh intentional PNG goldens, and run the repository's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]exhaustive landing gates.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-rs","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-rs.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-03414b97086824376ea5fc91bab93b9c","started_at":"2026-08-21T14:16:25.496072+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1787331310,"sha":"b88dfc729359edaf7bda546e6bf581c7f2266b07","subject":"fix(telemetry): drop duplicate sase_finalizer catalog entries"},{"committed_at":1787331436,"sha":"9223d47c4617075c6298c2dd4663b56ecb6281ac","subject":"feat(flags): a